39,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our past projects have struggled with timing. I found that works based on comfort or appeal often slip by a year, and weather has cost us many weeks of work.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh wow, I found something really important! It looks like our specialist rooms are mostly empty, but people are constantly being turned away from general-purpose rooms. We really need more flexible spaces for everyone!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are concerning. While some technicians have capacity, the grounds and front-of-house posts remain unfilled. Furthermore, our bench technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks that should be automated by the equipment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My research reveals a clear pattern: projects that benefit a single department are viewed as disappointments, while shared, bookable spaces receive the highest ratings. Also, older blocks contain hazardous materials that cause severe delays.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are equally sobering. Mechanical and ducted plant costs have surged by twenty percent, while we have neglected to create any renewal reserve for our aging audiovisual equipment. We are essentially planning for a future we cannot afford.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit worrying to see so many delays, isn't it? I feel for the poor workers who have to rush at the end when the weather doesn't cooperate. We should be very gentle with our planning.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, your findings match mine perfectly! It's so sad that some people are being turned away from rooms while others sit empty. We should definitely prioritize spaces that everyone can share and enjoy together!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, while shared spaces are a noble goal, we must consider who will actually manage them. If we add more general-purpose rooms without filling the vacant front-of-house posts, we are simply adding to the burden of an exhausted staff.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand your concern for the staff, but we cannot ignore that the current allocation of space is failing the users. We must find a solution that is both useful and manageable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, your concern for the staff is quite poignant. However, we must also acknowledge that our financial foundations are crumbling. If we invest in new spaces without a plan for equipment renewal, we are merely building expensive monuments to obsolescence.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, you have such a sharp eye for the numbers. Perhaps we can find a project that is modest in its needs, so we don't put too much pressure on our budget or our dear staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I totally hear you! We definitely don't want to make the staff's jobs harder. Maybe there's a way to create shared spaces that are easy to look after? I just want everyone to be happy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that is a kind thought, but ""easy to look after"" is often a misconception. My data shows technicians are already bogged down by manual routines because the equipment is failing them. We must prioritize efficiency over mere expansion.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, if the technicians are struggling with manual tasks, then a project that automates those routines or replaces failing equipment would be a logical priority. It would support the staff while improving overall utility.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, a logical priority indeed. However, we must be cautious; replacing equipment without a dedicated renewal reserve is a temporary fix. We risk repeating the same cycle of neglect that left our audiovisual kit in its current state.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I hope we can all find a way to be kind to our budget and our people. Perhaps a project that avoids the outdoors and doesn't promise too much ""appeal"" would be the most peaceful choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with Shizue! If we can find something that's helpful for the students but doesn't stress out the staff or the budget, that would be just wonderful. I'm sure there's a perfect middle ground!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,George,,"I believe the middle ground lies in reducing the current burden. If we can address the manual inefficiencies the technicians face, we provide relief to the staff while improving the facility's actual functionality. That is the only sustainable path.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, while I agree that staff relief is essential, we must also avoid the hazardous materials in the older blocks that I discovered. Any project we choose must be strategically located to avoid those costly and stressful delays.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are navigating a minefield of hazardous materials, staffing shortages, and financial fantasies. If we wish to avoid a catastrophe, we must select a project that avoids mechanical plant surges and doesn't rely on non-existent reserves.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
