64,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I feel that Candidate C, the Central Study Commons, is a very gentle choice. It is an indoor conversion, so our workers won't have to worry about the rain and frost.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I love Candidate C too! It's exactly what the data suggested—creating a shared, bookable space that everyone can use. It would be so wonderful to see those underused halls finally bringing people together!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,George,,"I must disagree. Candidate C adds a service desk, which requires front-of-house staff we simply do not have. Candidate D, however, addresses the manual burdens my technicians face by upgrading the failing extraction equipment.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, while D helps technicians, it involves heavy mechanical plant, which Benjamin noted is seeing a twenty percent cost surge. Candidate C is a conversion, but we must ensure it isn't in an older block with hazardous materials.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, your caution is well-placed. Candidate D is a financial fantasy given the surge in mechanical plant costs. Candidate B, meanwhile, is a trap; it relies on the very audiovisual kit for which we have no renewal reserve.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I understand your worry for the staff, but a service desk could perhaps be managed simply. Candidate A would be so stressful for the workers with all that outdoor weather.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I really don't want the staff to be stressed! But maybe the students could help out at the desk? Candidate C just feels so right because it helps so many people who are currently being turned away!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, relying on students for essential staffing is not a sustainable solution. It is a temporary patch for a systemic failure. Candidate D is the only option that actually removes a daily burden from our existing, overworked technicians.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, while I empathize with the technicians, we cannot ignore the financial reality Benjamin presented. Candidate D's cost surge makes it a liability. Candidate C is the most logical choice for user satisfaction and budget stability.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, while your desire to aid the technicians is noble, we cannot simply wish away a twenty percent increase in plant costs. Candidate D is a fiscal disaster waiting to happen. Candidate C, however, appears far more grounded.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is so heartening to see us talking through this. I worry that Candidate D might lead to the same rushing and stress I saw in the schedules, while Candidate C seems much more peaceful for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I really care about the technicians too, but if we pick D and it goes way over budget, that might cause even more stress for everyone! Candidate C makes so many people happy and feels like a win for the whole campus!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, happiness is fleeting if the foundation is crumbling. We are ignoring the people who keep this university running. If we choose C, we are simply adding another task to a depleted staff's list. D is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, we cannot prioritize one group's relief by risking a total project failure. Candidate D is fiscally irresponsible. Candidate C provides the shared utility the users desperately need and avoids the mechanical cost surges.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, your commitment to the staff is admirable, but logic dictates we cannot solve a staffing crisis by inviting a financial one. Candidate D is a recipe for a budget overrun that would leave us even more depleted. Candidate C is the only rational path.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I believe we have found a lovely consensus. Candidate C is the most considerate choice for our budget, our workers, and our students. I am happy to vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so glad we've found a way to make so many people happy! Candidate C is just perfect because it gives the students the space they need and keeps things stable. I vote for the Central Study Commons!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,George,,I cannot in good conscience support a plan that ignores the exhaustion of our staff. Adding a service desk to a depleted workforce is irresponsible. I stand by Candidate D as the only way to provide real relief. I vote for Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":44,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"While I respect George's dedication to the staff, we must prioritize a project that is actually viable. Candidate C aligns with user needs and avoids the financial and logistical risks of the other options. I vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a pity that George prefers a fiscal catastrophe to a staffing inconvenience. However, logic remains undefeated. Candidate C avoids the mechanical cost surges and the audiovisual void. I vote for the Central Study Commons.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
